        "## Summary and Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key Findings\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Precipitation Sensitivity**: The Aurora-Lite decoder system shows measurable sensitivity to temperature perturbations, with precipitation changes observable even from a localized 2.5K temperature anomaly.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Spatial Propagation**: The effects of the perturbation are not confined to the immediate vicinity of the temperature anomaly but can affect precipitation patterns across larger regions due to atmospheric dynamics.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Magnitude of Response**: The perturbation study reveals the model's ability to capture the nonlinear relationship between atmospheric temperature and hydrological processes.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Physical Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Temperature-Precipitation Coupling**: The applied perturbation simulates realistic atmospheric variability that can occur due to various meteorological processes\n",
        "- **Hydrological Cascade**: Changes in temperature affect not just precipitation but also evaporation, runoff, and soil moisture, demonstrating the interconnected nature of the water cycle\n",
        "- **Model Sensitivity**: The results show that the Aurora-Lite decoder system is sensitive enough to detect and propagate small-scale atmospheric perturbations\n",
        "\n",
        "### Applications\n",
        "\n",
        "This methodology can be used for:\n",
        "- **Sensitivity analysis** of weather prediction models\n",
        "- **Ensemble forecasting** by running multiple perturbation scenarios  \n",
        "- **Uncertainty quantification** in precipitation forecasts\n",
        "- **Climate impact studies** examining how small changes can lead to different outcomes"
