  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tzs9wk052xl",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Precipitation Perturbation Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This section implements a perturbation study to analyze how small atmospheric changes affect precipitation forecasts. We'll compare precipitation predictions from:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Baseline scenario**: Standard aurora-lite-decoder prediction without perturbations\n",
    "2. **Perturbed scenario**: Same prediction but with a small temperature perturbation applied\n",
    "\n",
    "## Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on the approach from PerturbationTries.ipynb, we apply a **Gaussian temperature perturbation** to specific atmospheric pressure levels (700-925 hPa). The perturbation is designed to represent realistic atmospheric variability:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Temperature change**: ΔT = (Lv × Δq) / cp\n",
    "  - Lv = 2.5×10⁶ J/kg (latent heat of vaporization)  \n",
    "  - cp = 1005 J/kg·K (specific heat at constant pressure)\n",
    "  - Δq = 0.001 (specific humidity perturbation)\n",
    "  - **Result**: ΔT ≈ 2.49 K maximum amplitude\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Spatial distribution**: Gaussian with σ = 8° centered at a chosen location\n",
    "- **Pressure levels**: Applied to 700, 850, and 925 hPa levels\n",
    "- **Temporal application**: Applied to both initial time steps (00:00 and 06:00)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b441lmzrqku",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Perturbation Parameters (from PerturbationTries.ipynb methodology)\n",
    "Lv = 2.5e6       # Latent heat of vaporization [J/kg]\n",
    "cp = 1005        # Specific heat at constant pressure [J/kg·K]\n",
    "delta_q = 0.0010 # Specific humidity perturbation\n",
    "delta_T = (Lv * delta_q) / cp  # Temperature perturbation amplitude\n",
    "sigma = 8.0      # Gaussian spread parameter (degrees)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Perturbation location (can be adjusted)\n",
    "center_lat = 60.0    # Latitude of perturbation center\n",
    "center_lon = -147.0  # Longitude of perturbation center (Alaska region)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pressure levels to apply perturbation (hPa)\n",
    "perturb_levels = [700, 850, 925]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Perturbation Parameters:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Temperature amplitude: {delta_T:.3f} K\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Gaussian sigma: {sigma}°\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Center location: ({center_lat}, {center_lon})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Pressure levels: {perturb_levels} hPa\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "zthj93snrhn",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def create_gaussian_perturbation_mask(lat_array, lon_array, center_lat, center_lon, sigma, amplitude):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Create a 2D Gaussian perturbation mask\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Parameters:\n",
    "    - lat_array, lon_array: coordinate arrays from the batch metadata\n",
    "    - center_lat, center_lon: center of the perturbation\n",
    "    - sigma: standard deviation of the Gaussian (degrees)\n",
    "    - amplitude: maximum amplitude of the perturbation\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "    - torch.Tensor: 2D perturbation mask [H, W]\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Handle longitude wrapping (ERA5 data uses 0-360° convention)\n",
    "    center_lon_adj = center_lon\n",
    "    if lon_array.max() > 180:\n",
    "        center_lon_adj = center_lon % 360\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Create meshgrid\n",
    "    LON, LAT = np.meshgrid(lon_array, lat_array)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Calculate distances\n",
    "    dlon = LON - center_lon_adj\n",
    "    dlat = LAT - center_lat\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Handle longitude wrapping for distance calculation\n",
    "    dlon = np.where(dlon > 180, dlon - 360, dlon)\n",
    "    dlon = np.where(dlon < -180, dlon + 360, dlon)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Create Gaussian mask\n",
    "    gaussian_mask = amplitude * np.exp(-(dlon**2 + dlat**2) / (2 * sigma**2))\n",
    "\n",
    "    return torch.from_numpy(gaussian_mask).float()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test the function with our batch data\n",
    "lat_array = batch.metadata.lat.numpy()\n",
    "lon_array = batch.metadata.lon.numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "gaussian_mask = create_gaussian_perturbation_mask(\n",
    "    lat_array, lon_array, center_lat, center_lon, sigma, delta_T\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Created Gaussian mask with shape: {gaussian_mask.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max perturbation amplitude: {gaussian_mask.max().item():.3f} K\")\n",
    "print(f\"Perturbation affects {(gaussian_mask > 0.01).sum()} grid points significantly (>0.01K)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wr2zyv5rgc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the perturbation mask\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot the perturbation mask\n",
    "im = ax.imshow(gaussian_mask.numpy(), extent=(-180, 180, -90, 90), \n",
    "               cmap='Reds', origin='upper')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mark the center point\n",
    "ax.plot(center_lon, center_lat, 'ko', markersize=10, label=f'Center ({center_lat}, {center_lon})')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add colorbar\n",
    "cbar = plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax, shrink=0.8)\n",
    "cbar.set_label('Temperature Perturbation (K)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Formatting\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Longitude (°)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Latitude (°)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Gaussian Temperature Perturbation Mask\\n(σ = {sigma}°, max ΔT = {delta_T:.2f} K)', fontsize=14)\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print some statistics about the mask\n",
    "mask_nonzero = gaussian_mask[gaussian_mask > 0.001]  # Values > 0.001 K\n",
    "print(f\"\\nPerturbation Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Grid points with ΔT > 0.001 K: {len(mask_nonzero)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean ΔT (non-zero points): {mask_nonzero.mean():.3f} K\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Standard deviation: {mask_nonzero.std():.3f} K\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "w0m0f092l5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Create Perturbed Batch\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we'll create a modified version of our input batch with the temperature perturbation applied to specific pressure levels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "urr3bg386il",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Store original batch as baseline\n",
    "batch_baseline = batch\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clone the temperature tensor for perturbation\n",
    "t_perturbed = batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"t\"].clone()  # shape: [B, T, L, H, W]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Original temperature tensor shape: {t_perturbed.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Available pressure levels: {batch_baseline.metadata.atmos_levels}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find indices for perturbation pressure levels\n",
    "p_levels = torch.tensor(batch_baseline.metadata.atmos_levels)\n",
    "perturb_indices = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for level in perturb_levels:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        idx = torch.where(p_levels == level)[0][0].item()\n",
    "        perturb_indices.append(idx)\n",
    "        print(f\"Found pressure level {level} hPa at index {idx}\")\n",
    "    except IndexError:\n",
    "        print(f\"Warning: Pressure level {level} hPa not found in data\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Will apply perturbation to indices: {perturb_indices}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply the Gaussian perturbation to selected pressure levels\n",
    "print(f\"\\nApplying perturbation...\")\n",
    "for idx in perturb_indices:\n",
    "    # Apply to both time steps (t=0 and t=1)\n",
    "    t_perturbed[0, :, idx] += gaussian_mask  # [Batch=0, Time=all, Level=idx, H, W]\n",
    "    print(f\"Applied perturbation to level index {idx} ({batch_baseline.metadata.atmos_levels[idx]} hPa)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check the magnitude of changes\n",
    "original_temp_sample = batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"t\"][0, 0, perturb_indices[0], 360, 720]  # Sample point\n",
    "perturbed_temp_sample = t_perturbed[0, 0, perturb_indices[0], 360, 720]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSample temperature change at center:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Original: {original_temp_sample:.2f} K\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Perturbed: {perturbed_temp_sample:.2f} K\") \n",
    "print(f\"  Change: {perturbed_temp_sample - original_temp_sample:.3f} K\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "icrfejusoi",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create the perturbed batch\n",
    "batch_perturbed = Batch(\n",
    "    surf_vars=batch_baseline.surf_vars,  # Keep surface variables unchanged\n",
    "    static_vars=batch_baseline.static_vars,  # Keep static variables unchanged\n",
    "    atmos_vars={\n",
    "        \"t\": t_perturbed,  # Use perturbed temperature\n",
    "        \"u\": batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"u\"],  # Keep u-wind unchanged\n",
    "        \"v\": batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"v\"],  # Keep v-wind unchanged\n",
    "        \"q\": batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"q\"],  # Keep specific humidity unchanged\n",
    "        \"z\": batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"z\"],  # Keep geopotential unchanged\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    metadata=batch_baseline.metadata,  # Keep metadata unchanged\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Successfully created perturbed batch!\")\n",
    "print(f\"Baseline batch shape: {batch_baseline.atmos_vars['t'].shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Perturbed batch shape: {batch_perturbed.atmos_vars['t'].shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify that only temperature is different\n",
    "temp_diff = torch.abs(batch_perturbed.atmos_vars[\"t\"] - batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"t\"])\n",
    "u_diff = torch.abs(batch_perturbed.atmos_vars[\"u\"] - batch_baseline.atmos_vars[\"u\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nVerification:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Temperature max difference: {temp_diff.max():.3f} K\")\n",
    "print(f\"  U-wind max difference: {u_diff.max():.6f} m/s (should be 0)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Temperature changed at {(temp_diff > 1e-6).sum()} grid points\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ppauprnz7t8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Run Predictions for Both Scenarios\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we'll run the Aurora-Lite model and decoders for both the baseline and perturbed scenarios to compare the precipitation forecasts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2dsby0qe7yj",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Running Aurora-Lite predictions...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run baseline prediction (no perturbation)\n",
    "print(\"1. Baseline scenario (no perturbation):\")\n",
    "with torch.inference_mode():\n",
    "    preds_baseline, lat_dec_baseline = modelAurora.forward(batch_baseline)\n",
    "    latent_decoder_baseline = lat_dec_baseline.detach().clone()\n",
    "    preds_new_baseline = modelDecoder.forward(latent_decoder_baseline, \n",
    "                                            batch_baseline.metadata.lat, \n",
    "                                            batch_baseline.metadata.lon)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Transform baseline predictions\n",
    "preds_baseline_transformed = {k: transform_data(v.cpu().numpy().squeeze(), k, direct=False) \n",
    "                             for k, v in preds_new_baseline.items()}\n",
    "print(\"   ✓ Baseline prediction completed\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run perturbed prediction\n",
    "print(\"2. Perturbed scenario:\")\n",
    "with torch.inference_mode():\n",
    "    preds_perturbed, lat_dec_perturbed = modelAurora.forward(batch_perturbed)\n",
    "    latent_decoder_perturbed = lat_dec_perturbed.detach().clone()\n",
    "    preds_new_perturbed = modelDecoder.forward(latent_decoder_perturbed,\n",
    "                                             batch_perturbed.metadata.lat,\n",
    "                                             batch_perturbed.metadata.lon)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Transform perturbed predictions\n",
    "preds_perturbed_transformed = {k: transform_data(v.cpu().numpy().squeeze(), k, direct=False) \n",
    "                              for k, v in preds_new_perturbed.items()}\n",
    "print(\"   ✓ Perturbed prediction completed\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPrediction summary:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Variables predicted: {list(preds_baseline_transformed.keys())}\")\n",
    "for var in preds_baseline_transformed.keys():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {var} shape: {preds_baseline_transformed[var].shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clear some memory\n",
    "torch.cuda.empty_cache()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6pascgjlmgv",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Precipitation Change Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's analyze how the temperature perturbation affected the precipitation forecast."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6g93aetqv0a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract precipitation data\n",
    "precip_baseline = preds_baseline_transformed['tp_mswep']  # mm/6h\n",
    "precip_perturbed = preds_perturbed_transformed['tp_mswep']  # mm/6h\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate differences\n",
    "precip_diff = precip_perturbed - precip_baseline  # mm/6h\n",
    "precip_rel_diff = np.where(precip_baseline > 1e-6,  # Avoid division by very small numbers\n",
    "                          (precip_diff / precip_baseline) * 100, \n",
    "                          0)  # Relative difference in %\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Precipitation Change Analysis\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 40)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Basic statistics\n",
    "print(f\"Baseline Precipitation Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(precip_baseline):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Max: {np.max(precip_baseline):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total: {np.sum(precip_baseline):.2f} mm\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Grid points with precip > 0.1 mm/6h: {(precip_baseline > 0.1e-3).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nPerturbed Precipitation Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(precip_perturbed):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Max: {np.max(precip_perturbed):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total: {np.sum(precip_perturbed):.2f} mm\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Grid points with precip > 0.1 mm/6h: {(precip_perturbed > 0.1e-3).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nPrecipitation Change Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Max increase: {np.max(precip_diff):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Max decrease: {np.min(precip_diff):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean change: {np.mean(precip_diff):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
    "print(f\"  RMS change: {np.sqrt(np.mean(precip_diff**2)):.4f} mm/6h\")\n",
